<http://data.silknow.org/object/ff77541f-19ef-37f1-af39-a1f98cb8d824/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Hanging. Linen embroidered with silk in atma, chain and Cretan stitch (stems) and double running in a line (at the tops of the crescents).\nMade from three widths of black linen: that on the right was joined before being embroidered; that on the left was joined after being embroidered.\nThe black border is a floral meander with a thick green stem which joines red flowers with a white centre. A blue tulip with white cresecent chintamani alternate between the flowers with a yellow leaf and white crescent chintamani.\nThe black field is decorated with green zigzagged parallel stems.  These bear pairs of leaves: one red containing a small sprig with a pair of flowers and a tulip, a one yellow containing a similar small flower above and below a tulip.The pairs of leaves alternate in direction along the stem. the stem also bears a small yellow stem with a blue spiky leaf and a red leaf with three white petals."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/ff77541f-19ef-37f1-af39-a1f98cb8d824> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/ff77541f-19ef-37f1-af39-a1f98cb8d824/dimension/1>
